  "term": "medial temporal lobe",
  "definition": "The medial temporal lobe is a set of brain regions linked to declarative memory, meaning memory for facts and events. In psychology and neuroscience contexts, it is discussed as an important neural basis of memory abilities, including memory for observed visual scenes.",
